      "content": "Bad Bunny beat First General London 6-2 \u2014 and the Group Chat Will Hear About It\n\n2 finalized games, 15 verified goals, and no mercy from the standings table.\n\nHockey Life closed the books on 2 games from 2026-09-28 through 2026-10-04. Every score below comes from the finalized game record.\n\nThe widest gap was 4 goals, which is less a margin than a request for somebody to locate the backcheck.\n\nTHIS WEEK ON THE ICE\n\nFitzRays Flyers 4, Liuna Premier 3\n\nFitzRays Flyers Takes the Points and Leaves the Tape Bill\n\nFitzRays Flyers beat Liuna Premier 4-3.\n\nThe margin stayed tight enough that every missed clearance came with its own tiny courtroom drama.\n\nThe verified scoresheet credits Jack Foote (2G, 1A); Steve Almond (1G, 1A); Cameron Sheppard (1G, 0A); Cooper Hatfield (1G, 0A).\n\nBad Bunny 6, First General London 2\n\nBad Bunny Turns the Scoreboard Into a Complaint Form\n\nBad Bunny beat First General London 6-2.\n\nA 4-goal margin is not a defensive system; it is an open invitation with free parking.\n\nThe verified scoresheet credits Trevor Paterson (2G, 1A); Adrian Hartley (1G, 1A); Eric Hartley (1G, 1A); Jonathan Brougham (1G, 1A).\n\nTHREE STARS OF THE WEEK\n\n1. Jack Foote, FitzRays Flyers: 3 verified points across the covered games (2 goals, 1 assists).\n\n2. Trevor Paterson, Bad Bunny: 3 verified points across the covered games (2 goals, 1 assists).\n\n3. Adrian Hartley, Bad Bunny: 2 verified points across the covered games (1 goals, 1 assists).\n\nTHIS WEEK BY THE NUMBERS\n\nFinalized games: 2 \u2014 All games in the selected period were checked before generation.\n\nGoals: 15 \u2014 Combined final-score total.\n\nBiggest margin: 4 \u2014 Calculated from verified final scores.\n\nSTANDINGS\n\nBad Bunny: 1 GP, 1-0-0-0, 2 PTS, 6 GF, 2 GA\n\nFitzRays Flyers: 1 GP, 1-0-0-0, 2 PTS, 4 GF, 3 GA\n\nLiuna Premier: 1 GP, 0-1-0-0, 0 PTS, 3 GF, 4 GA\n\nFirst General London: 1 GP, 0-1-0-0, 0 PTS, 2 GF, 6 GA\n\nCanonical season standings at generation time.\n\nTHE HEATER\n\nBad Bunny Owns the Top Line: 2 points through 1 games. The standings do not award style points, which is convenient because they already have the real ones.\n\nTHE COLD TUB\n\nFirst General London Has Located the Basement: 0 points with 6 goals against. The thermostat works; the defensive coverage may need a service call.\n\nNEXT WEEK HEADLINES\n\nLiuna Premier at Bad Bunny: Scheduled matchup. No result, attendance, or performance claim is made before the puck drops.\n\nFirst General London at FitzRays Flyers: Scheduled matchup. No result, attendance, or performance claim is made before the puck drops.",
